  "discussion": "A small, medium-period northwest swell will provide a small boost to surf along north-facing shores on Friday. A moderate, medium-period north-northwest swell will build late Saturday and peak around seasonal average on Sunday. As this swell declines on Monday, a long- period west-northwest swell will arrive, maintaining moderate surf through the middle of next week. Small background level surf will prevail along south-facing shores through Friday. A small to moderate, south-southwesterly swell is expected to boost surf to around seasonal average this weekend into early next week. Along east-facing shores, trade-wind swell will decrease today, though a small, medium-period northeast swell may maintain small surf through Saturday. Aside from wrapping north-northwest swell in exposed areas, east shore surf should remain below seasonal average much of next week.",
